invariant: INV-14
file: quic_token.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the tag input keeps the address's length byte and drops its bytes,
  so a token minted for one client checks at any other address of the same
  length. An attacker that obtains a token at its own address can then
  spend it from a spoofed one, which is the amplification RFC 9000 section
  8.1.4 asks a Retry token to prevent. The address case in
  test/quic_token_tests.h moves the port by one and changes the address's
  first byte, and requires both to be refused.

--- old
    wb_bytes(&w, address, address_len);
--- new
    wb_bytes(&w, address, 0);
